/-! # Generic flatness and finite presentation over a reduced affine base

Source: Stacks Project, Morphisms, Tag 052B (proposition-generic-flatness-reduced),
structure-sheaf case with affine source and target
(blueprint: lem-sfb-reduced-affine-generic-flat-finite-presentation).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Topology

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A locally finite type morphism between affine schemes with reduced target becomes flat
and locally of finite presentation over a dense open subscheme of the target.

Source: Stacks Project, Morphisms, Tag 052B (proposition-generic-flatness-reduced),
structure-sheaf case with affine source and target
(blueprint: lem-sfb-reduced-affine-generic-flat-finite-presentation).

Proof:
1. Write the morphism as Spec of a ring map A → B using `def-weil-affine-spectrum`.
By `lem-weil-pbc-affine-scheme-reduced-iff`, A is reduced. By
`lem-weil-pbc-lft-affine-pairs`, B is a finite type A-algebra. Choose a surjection
q : P = A[x₁,...,xₙ] → B using `def-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra`.
2. As a P-module via q, B is generated by 1. Apply
`lem-sfb-reduced-polynomial-module-generic-freeness` to this cyclic module.
Its good locus is a dense open D, the union of the principal opens D(f) where B_f is
free over A_f and finitely presented over P_f = A_f[x₁,...,xₙ]. The notions of finite
generation and localization are `def-weil-finitely-generated-module`,
`def-weil-ring-localization-away`, and `def-weil-pbc-module-localization-away`.
Localization of the underlying A-module agrees with the underlying module of the
localized algebra: both have fractions b/φ(f)^a with the same equality relation.
3. On each good D(f), the induced q_f : P_f → B_f is surjective: lift the numerator
of a fraction using q, then divide by f to the same power. Regard q_f as P_f-linear.
By `lem-trf-finite-presentation-surjective-module-kernel`, its kernel is finitely
generated as a P_f-module, since P_f is cyclic and B_f finitely presented.
These module generators also generate the kernel ideal. Quotienting P_f by this
finitely generated ideal gives B_f, by the kernel criterion and surjectivity.
This is the finite algebra presentation of `def-weil-pbc-finitely-presented-algebra`.
4. The same B_f is free over A_f by step 2. It is flat by the explicit free-module
clause of `lem-weil-pbc-projective-module-flat`.
5. For any open D of V, the inverse-image open g⁻¹(D), with its restricted sheaf,
represents U ×_V D: a compatible pair of maps into U and D uniquely factors through
this open, and restriction of the sheaf map gives the unique morphism into it.
Conversely this morphism gives the compatible pair. Thus the universal property in
`def-pc-fibre-product` identifies its map to D with the base-change projection.
The restricted scheme and its inclusion use `def-weil-open-immersion`.
6. For a good f, `lem-weil-pbc-basic-open-pullback` identifies g⁻¹(D(f)) with D(φ(f)).
By `lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-section-vanishing-prime`, their rings are B_f and A_f.
Their section map sends a/f^k to φ(a)/φ(f)^k, since restriction preserves a/1 and
ring maps preserve inverses. Step 4 and `lem-weil-pbc-flat-ring-map-iff-flat-affine`
give flatness of this chart morphism; step 3 gives its finite algebra presentation.
7. Each point of g⁻¹(D) maps into a good D(f). The corresponding affine source and
target neighbourhoods from step 6 give local finite presentation, by
`def-sbc-locally-finite-presentation`, and flatness of the local-ring map, by
`def-weil-flat-morphism`. Restriction to opens preserves these local rings and maps,
by `def-weil-open-immersion`. Hence the map to D has both properties. Step 5
identifies it with the stated projection. For an empty V the dense open is empty
and the pointwise assertions are vacuous; an empty U causes no exception either.
-/
theorem exists_dense_open_flat_locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_isReduced_affine
    {U V : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine U] [IsAffine V] [IsReduced V]
    (g : U ⟶ V) [LocallyOfFiniteType g] :
    ∃ D : V.Opens, Dense (D : Set V) ∧ Flat (pullback.snd g D.ι) ∧
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation (pullback.snd g D.ι) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
